From 3d1ba8aa9fb08400870bcfa67f21e5af812c0314 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Corvid <corvid@example.invalid>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 11:24:09 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] FFmpeg 9.0.2 for Corvid (redistributable)

- contrib/ffmpeg-9.0-jsonstats.patch: the JSON progress report ported to
  the threaded fftools of FFmpeg 7 and later (same lines and fields).
- contrib/ffmpeg-9.0-hls.patch: the HLS muxer extensions for 9.0.
- Dockerfile.ubuntu.corvid: no --enable-nonfree; the CUDA filters are
  built with clang (--enable-cuda-llvm), no CUDA toolkit and no
  libfdk-aac/libnpp. NVENC/NVDEC headers 12.1.14.0 (driver >= 530).
  The 'bundle' target produces a self-contained ffmpeg ($ORIGIN/lib)
  for the Corvid update package.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UhjysExATCKDyVfUWLA89B
---
